<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Package xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
    Companion manifest for manifest/portfolio-deal-b4/destructiveChangesPost.xml.

    STATUS: PREPARED, NOT AUTHORISED. Do not deploy without the user's explicit
    go-ahead.

    Phase B4 of the "Property Package -> Portfolio Deal" rename program renames
    6 Apex classes and 2 LWC bundles (an Apex/LWC rename is delete-and-create,
    there is no in-place rename at the Metadata API level) and repoints every
    caller at the new names. This org (usman-dpeg, live, no source tracking) has
    no mechanism to delete the old components on its own -- a plain
    `--source-dir` deploy only adds/updates what's present locally -- so the old
    components must be removed via the companion destructiveChangesPost.xml in
    the SAME transaction as this package.xml. See that file for the deletion
    list and rationale.

    Verified fresh for B4 via `git status`/`git diff` against the working tree
    (2026-08-18), not assumed from the original task brief -- the brief's guess
    at which permission sets carry "comment-only touch-ups" undercounted both the
    number of sets touched and the substance of the touch: all 5 permission sets
    below currently carry real, uncommitted Portfolio_Deal__c grants (additive
    field/object permissions from Phases B1/B2, not yet deployed to the org) in
    addition to whatever B4 itself changed on them. All 5 are included here so
    the whole Portfolio_Deal__c permission surface lands atomically with the
    Apex/LWC rename rather than in a partial, inconsistent state:
      - DPEG_Apex_Access: HARD DEPENDENCY. Its classAccesses entry is repointed
        from PropertyPackageController to PortfolioDealController. A
        classAccesses entry naming a class that no longer exists fails the
        deploy of the whole permission set, so this MUST land in the same
        transaction as the class rename and the destructive deletion below.
      - DPEG_Admin_Access, DPEG_Acquisition_Edit, DPEG_Acquisition_View,
        Broker_Protection_Access: each carries real (non-comment-only)
        Portfolio_Deal__c field/object permission grants dated Phase B1/B2
        2026-08-18, plus comment updates naming the renamed B4 widgets
        (c/recentPortfolioDeals, c/portfolioDealSiblings). None of these has a
        hard technical dependency on the destructive deletion the way
        DPEG_Apex_Access does, but bundling them keeps one coherent,
        atomically-landed permission story for Portfolio_Deal__c rather than
        splitting an already-multi-phase rename across still more separate
        deploys.

    Also carries the comment-only rewrite to c/recentLeads (js + its Jest test),
    which references the renamed c/recentPackages -> c/recentPortfolioDeals
    widget in explanatory comments only -- confirmed via diff that every added
    line in both files is a comment or blank line, no functional or test-
    behaviour change. Bundled here for the same reason A3 bundled its 6
    comment-only components: deploy-time no-op, included so the transaction is
    atomic, not because anything below depends on it.

    ApexClass (17):
      6 NEW (the B4 rename targets):
        - PortfolioDealController      (was PropertyPackageController)
        - PortfolioDealControllerTest  (was PropertyPackageControllerTest)
        - PortfolioDealSelector        (was PropertyPackageSelector)
        - PortfolioDealSelectorTest    (was PropertyPackageSelectorTest)
        - PortfolioDealService         (was PropertyPackageService)
        - PortfolioDealServiceTest     (was PropertyPackageServiceTest)
      11 REPOINTED (unchanged names, updated to call the new classes / select
      the new object):
        - LeadSelector, LeadSelectorTest
        - OpportunitySelector
        - LeadFunnelController, LeadFunnelControllerTest
        - EmailToLeadService, EmailToLeadServiceTest
        - ExtractAddressQueueable, ExtractAddressQueueableTest
        - LeadConvertService, LeadConvertServiceTest

    LightningComponentBundle (3):
      - recentPortfolioDeals   (new, was recentPackages)
      - portfolioDealSiblings  (new, was packageSiblings)
      - recentLeads            (comment-only touch-up, see above)

    Flexipage (3): repointed to the renamed LWC bundles
      - Lead_Funnel
      - Lead_Record_Page
      - Opportunity_Record_Page

    PermissionSet (5): see the verification note above
      - DPEG_Apex_Access
      - DPEG_Admin_Access
      - DPEG_Acquisition_Edit
      - DPEG_Acquisition_View
      - Broker_Protection_Access

    Deploy (only once authorised by the user; devops runs a validation-only
    dry-run first per standing project practice):
      sf project deploy start \
        --manifest manifest/portfolio-deal-b4/package.xml \
        --post-destructive-changes manifest/portfolio-deal-b4/destructiveChangesPost.xml \
        --target-org usman-dpeg \
        --test-level RunLocalTests --wait 30

    Do NOT pass --purge-on-delete -- documented as non-functional on production
    orgs and fails silently rather than erroring (see manifest/portfolio-deal-a3).
    -->
    <types>
        <members>PortfolioDealController</members>
        <members>PortfolioDealControllerTest</members>
        <members>PortfolioDealSelector</members>
        <members>PortfolioDealSelectorTest</members>
        <members>PortfolioDealService</members>
        <members>PortfolioDealServiceTest</members>
        <members>LeadSelector</members>
        <members>LeadSelectorTest</members>
        <members>OpportunitySelector</members>
        <members>LeadFunnelController</members>
        <members>LeadFunnelControllerTest</members>
        <members>EmailToLeadService</members>
        <members>EmailToLeadServiceTest</members>
        <members>ExtractAddressQueueable</members>
        <members>ExtractAddressQueueableTest</members>
        <members>LeadConvertService</members>
        <members>LeadConvertServiceTest</members>
        <name>ApexClass</name>
    </types>
    <types>
        <members>recentPortfolioDeals</members>
        <members>portfolioDealSiblings</members>
        <members>recentLeads</members>
        <name>LightningComponentBundle</name>
    </types>
    <types>
        <members>Lead_Funnel</members>
        <members>Lead_Record_Page</members>
        <members>Opportunity_Record_Page</members>
        <name>Flexipage</name>
    </types>
    <types>
        <members>DPEG_Apex_Access</members>
        <members>DPEG_Admin_Access</members>
        <members>DPEG_Acquisition_Edit</members>
        <members>DPEG_Acquisition_View</members>
        <members>Broker_Protection_Access</members>
        <name>PermissionSet</name>
    </types>
    <version>67.0</version>
</Package>
